    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d918">

                <pb facs="0835" n="719" xml:id="pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2751.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Consul at Juárez.
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department approves your proposed action, as stated in your telegram February 7,
                    concerning protest to anti-Maderists now in power at Casas Grandes against
                    taking firearms from Americans. You should make your protest emphatic, and base
                    it on the ground that Americans must not be left without means of defense to
                    protect themselves during the present unsettled conditions against marauding
                    robbers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
